cli-administration-wait-needed = --wait needs seconds
cli-administration-wait-range = --wait must be 0..86400 seconds
cli-administration-secret-fd-needed = Secret descriptor number is missing
cli-administration-secret-fd-invalid = Secret descriptor must be a nonnegative integer
cli-administration-no-secret-values = Passwords and configuration text cannot be command-line values; use --password-fd or --input
cli-administration-no-target = This operation does not take a target
cli-administration-invalid-port = Invalid TCP/UDP port or range
cli-administration-unknown-group = Unknown management group
cli-administration-missing-inventory = Authorized inspection returned no inventory
cli-administration-missing-target = The target is not in the current list; refresh and use its exact ID
cli-administration-several-targets = Several items match; choose an exact ID from the list
cli-administration-unavailable-action = This action is unavailable for the target; inspect its current details
cli-administration-review-needed = Review this change, then pass --yes
cli-administration-wait-stopped = Stopped waiting; the operation may still be running. Use operations attach with its ID.
cli-administration-usage = Usage: tundra-cli { $group } <operation> [target] [options]
cli-administration-options = --json  --yes  --non-interactive  --wait <0..86400 seconds> (default 900)
cli-administration-secret-help = --password-fd <fd> reads the operation password; --authorization-fd <fd> reads the sudo password. Secrets are never arguments.
cli-administration-exit-codes = Exit codes: 0 success; 1 failure/partial; 2 arguments; 3 permission; 4 unsupported; 5 busy/version conflict; 6 input needed; 7 unfinished/unknown; 130 cancelled.
cli-administration-help-firewall = list; show RULE_ID; listeners [--filter TEXT --authorize]; allow --port PORT_OR_RANGE [--protocol tcp|udp --source IP_OR_CIDR --zone ZONE --duration runtime|permanent|both]; remove RULE_ID. Only existing UFW/firewalld are supported. No automatic install or enable. UFW changes are immediate and permanent together; inactive UFW only saves rules.
cli-administration-help-ssh = show/keys [USER] [--authorize]; configure [USER] [--port PORT --password-authentication yes|no --pubkey-authentication yes|no --permit-root-login yes|prohibit-password|forced-commands-only|no --open-firewall true|false]; add-key USER --public-key 'ssh-ed25519 ...'; remove-key USER --fingerprint SHA256:...; status/confirm/cancel TRANSACTION_ID. Configuration waits up to 120 seconds for confirm from a new real SSH connection; do not close the original command. Firewall sync defaults to false and preserves old ports.
cli-administration-help-backups = list [--filter TEXT]; show/preview-restore ID; restore ID [--allow-unvalidated]. Protected history requests authorization. Recovery checks current files and refuses external changes; restored operations create their own recovery records.
cli-administration-help-scheduled-tasks = list [--filter TEXT --authorize]; inspect TASK_ID; preview/create --name NAME --command 'literal shell command' --schedule 'systemd calendar' [--working-directory PATH --user USER]; pause/resume/run-now TASK_ID. New tasks use system time, retain their service/timer definitions, and do not replay missed triggers. Cron scheduled runs have no recorded exit status; manual results are separate.
cli-administration-root-usage = Usage: tundra-cli <config|launcher|services|processes|packages|network|disks|users|firewall|ssh|backups|scheduled-tasks|system-config|operations|logs|debug|cls|new|repl|help>
